<title>CROATIA: Croatian Sept crude output down, natural gas rises.</title>
<headline>Croatian Sept crude output down, natural gas rises.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA OIL EXTRACTION	 SEPTEMBER    AUGUST     SEPT '95</p>
<p> Crude petroleum (tonnes)	115,763    122,972     103,449</p>
<p> Natural gas (000 cu m)	  156,485    147,980	90,361</p>
<p>PETROLEUM PRODUCTS (tonnes)</p>
<p> Gasoline			     69,703    124,016     110,188</p>
<p> Gas oil				17,927     68,833	50,374</p>
<p> Heating oil			 116,601    121,512     147,353</p>
<p>NOTES -- Data excludes production from Serb-held Eastern Slavonia, where production was partly restarted on some oilfields late in August.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom +385 1 4557075</p>
</text>
